    "created_at": "2016-03-01T15:43:25Z",
    "updated_at": "2016-03-01T15:43:25Z",
    "body": "I don't think there's a need to be consistent there. Transfer doesn't have a fallback case, so it's very different from cloning in terms of who needs to define what. If we gave all objects these internal methods, that wouldn't change things either; the fallback case would still apply to new objects, unless they were defined to explicitly override the default own-properties [[Clone]].\n",
    "author_association": "MEMBER",
    "pin": null,
