    "created_at": "2016-03-01T16:11:13Z",
    "updated_at": "2016-03-01T16:11:13Z",
    "body": "For the record, @annevk and I spelunked through Firefox's implementation a bit. Key lines are:\n- https://mxr.mozilla.org/mozilla-central/source/js/src/jsfriendapi.cpp#267 which sets an object's \"JS class\" to \"Object\" if it's a \"plain object\"\n- https://mxr.mozilla.org/mozilla-central/source/js/src/vm/StructuredClone.cpp#1178 which keys off of that to do the own-property cloning instead of saying unsupported\n\nThis notion of \"plain object\" isn't something terribly well supported by the ES spec, but maybe \"has no internal slots\" is a good proxy for it. (In ES5 it was taken care of by [[Class]] being Object.)\n",
    "author_association": "MEMBER",
    "pin": null,
