    "created_at": "2016-03-01T19:57:05Z",
    "updated_at": "2016-03-01T19:57:05Z",
    "body": "Not sure what you mean by \"feasible\". Any choice here should be implementable. Mostly Chrome's behavior can be explained by the fact that the structured clone code is in Blink and the new ES object code is in V8. So it's really a matter of what we'd like to say in the spec. From that point of view, I guess it's more concise to say \"has internal slots\" (though I don't know how that interacts with, say, the private state proposal).\n",
